//! Composing and sending mail — the switch point.
//!
//! Gmail has no structured send. `users.messages.send` takes one field, `raw`,
//! holding a complete RFC822 message in base64url. Everything a reply needs to
//! thread correctly in *somebody else's* client — `In-Reply-To`, `References`,
//! a `Re:` that has not stacked, an RFC 2047 encoded subject — has to be right
//! in those bytes, because nothing downstream will fix it. That is why this is
//! a module with tests over the generated bytes rather than a function that
//! calls a builder.
//!
//! # Layout
//!
//! | module | what lives there |
//! |---|---|
//! | [`address`] | recipient arithmetic: reply-all, dedupe, exclude self |
//! | [`markdown`] | the markdown-ish editor grammar → clean HTML |
//! | [`mime`] | [`Outgoing`] → RFC822 bytes |
//! | [`draft`] | drafts, autosave, and building a reply from a stored thread |
//! | [`outbox`] | the ten-second undo window and the durable send queue |
//!
//! # Three decisions worth knowing
//!
//! **Address headers are rendered here, not by `mail-builder`.** The crate
//! builds the message structure, the body encoding and every other header, but
//! its `rfc2047_encode` wraps an encoded display name in double quotes —
//! `"=?utf-8?B?Sm9zw6k=?=" <jose@…>` — and RFC 2047 §5 forbids encoded-words
//! inside a quoted-string. Most clients decode it anyway; "most" is not the bar
//! for the header that carries your name into other people's inboxes. See
//! [`mime::render_mailboxes`].
//!
//! **The outbox is a table, not a timer.** A ten-second undo window implemented
//! as a `setTimeout` loses the message if the window closes inside it. Here the
//! finished RFC822 bytes are committed to SQLite *before* the window opens, so
//! the only thing the timer decides is when a durable row is allowed to leave.
//! Undo deletes the row; a crash leaves it, and the next flush sends it.
//!
//! **This module owns its own tables.** `db::schema` belongs to another unit,
//! so [`ensure_compose_schema`] creates `compose_drafts` and `compose_outbox`
//! with `CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS`, exactly as
//! [`command_queries::ensure_command_schema`](crate::db::command_queries::ensure_command_schema)
//! does for `snoozed_threads`. Promoting them into `MIGRATIONS` later is a
//! no-op for this call.

